      "html": "<ul><li>Type: stem plant</li><li>Origin: Asia</li><li>Height: 20–30+ cm</li><li>Light demand: low</li><li>CO2 demand: medium</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cardaminelyrata(024)/4441",
      "html": "<p>Plant it in groups, and make sure the water temperature does not exceed 28 °C (this makes the leaves much smaller and the plant more leggy).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cardaminelyrata(024)/4441",
      "html": "<p>Cardamine lyrata is actually a marsh plant from Japan. But it is also a familiar aquarium plant which thrives under water with 20–50 cm long stems. A characteristic trailing growth form makes it highly decorative, and 'aerial' roots often form on the plant itself. Also suitable in garden ponds in the summer.</p>"
    }
  ],
